==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|blunder}}, {{m|enm|blonder||disturbance, strife}}, from the verb {{m|enm|blundren}}, {{m|enm|blondren}}, which itself is partly from {{inh|en|enm|blondren}}, a frequentative form of {{m|enm|blonden}}, {{m|enm|blanden}} {{gloss|"to mix; mix up"; see {{l|en|blend}}}}; and partly from {{m|enm|blundren}}, a frequentative form of {{m|enm|blunden||to stagger; stumble}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|blunda||to shut the eyes; doze}}. Cognates include Norwegian {{m|no|blunda||to shut the eyes; doze}}, Swedish dialectal {{m|sv|blundra||to act blindly or rashly}}, Danish {{m|da|blunde||to blink}} or {{m|da|blunde||to take a nap}}.

