===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make a clumsy or stupid mistake.
#: ''to '''blunder''' in preparing a medical prescription''
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To move [[blindly]] or [[clumsily]].
#* Goldsmith
#*: I was never distinguished for address, and have often even '''blundered''' in making my bow.
#* Dryden
#*: '''blunders''' on, and staggers every pace
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to make a mistake.
#* Ditton
#*: To '''blunder''' an adversary.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To do or treat in a blundering manner; to confuse.
#* Stillingfleet
#*: He '''blunders''' and confounds all these together.

